  speakerName: Kalaw
  speakerPortrait: {fileID: 0}
  dialogueText: 'Once you''ve greeted someone, you can show more warmth by asking
    how they are.

    In Ilokano, ''kumusta ka?'' means ''how are you?''

    You
    can use it when checking on a friend, neighbor, or someone you''ve just met.

    Listen
    carefully: kumusta ka?

    Now, try saying ''kumusta ka?'' yourself.'
